  "retrieved_at": "2026-10-05",
  "difficulty_level": "H2",
  "difficulty_reason": "After the elementary convexity of a higher rank Voronoi cell and the induced filtration are supplied, the authors must still recover the whole closure of the cell from the scalar Voronoi cells of the successive graded projections. The inclusion is extracted coordinate by coordinate from the lexicographic inequalities using the Lifting Lemma, and the reverse inclusion is proved through strict inequalities on products of interiors of the scalar cells, together with the translated-set reduction for a general site. The mechanism is the interaction of a lexicographic order with an almost orthogonal decomposition that need not be orthogonal, and it is precisely the structural statement explaining why higher rank Voronoi cells fail to be closed; this is research-level asymptotic convex and polyhedral geometry, not a qualification exercise.",
